  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global program on climate-resilient renewable energy systems in SIDS # national project in Saint Lucia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The national project in Saint Lucia is part of the GEF and bilateral donor (e.g. Government of Austria) funded Global Program on Climate Resilient Renewable Energy Systems (G-RES), coordinated by UNIDO with the involvement of the Global Network of Regional Sustainable Energy Centres (GN-SEC) and other SIDS partners (see program component under Project ID. 250231).  The global program promotes climate-resilient renewable energy systems in SIDS to strengthen energy security, reduce GHG emissions and dependence on fossil fuels, achieve long-term economic savings from avoided climate-related losses, and deliver adaptation co-benefits for key sectors such as water, agriculture, tourism, as well as the blue economy.  The program comprises a global-regional component and individual national &quot;child projects&quot; to be executed in partnership with national institutions. The global-regional component to be executed by UNIDO and the GN-SEC centres will build coherence across the national projects and foster accelerated progress through regional and SIDS-SIDS cooperation, knowledge exchange and technology transfer.  After presenting the program, the Government of Saint Lucia has expressed interest to become part of it and provided an endorsement letter for a national &quot;child project&quot;, which will focus on the adoption and provis</narrative>
  </description>
